To create an HTML page that waits a specific amount of time before triggering an action, you can use JavaScript’s `setTimeout` function. This is useful for creating splash screens, loading animations, or delayed popups.

Here’s an example HTML code that waits for 5 seconds before displaying a popup message:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Delayed Action Example</title>
    <style>
        /* Centered message box styling */
        .popup {
            display: none;
            position: fixed;
            top: 50%;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: #333;
            color: #fff;
            border-radius: 8px;
            text-align: center;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
        }
        /* Close button styling */
        .close-btn {
            background-color: red;
            color: white;
            padding: 5px 10px;
            border: none;
            cursor: pointer;
            margin-top: 10px;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        .close-btn:hover {
            background-color: darkred;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div id="popup" class="popup">
    <p>This message appeared after a 5-second delay!</p>
    <button class="close-btn" onclick="closePopup()">Close</button>
</div>

<script>
    // Function to show the popup after a delay
    function showPopup() {
        document.getElementById('popup').style.display = 'block';
    }

    // Function to close the popup
    function closePopup() {
        document.getElementById('popup').style.display = 'none';
    }

    // Set a delay of 5 seconds (5000 milliseconds) before showing the popup
    setTimeout(showPopup, 5000);
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
1. **`setTimeout(showPopup, 5000);`**: This function waits for 5 seconds (5000 milliseconds) before executing the `showPopup` function.
2. **Popup Styling**: The popup (`#popup`) is hidden by default (`display: none`). After the timeout, it is displayed in the center of the page.
3. **Close Button**: The close button allows users to manually close the popup by calling the `closePopup` function.

### Customization:
- **Delay Time**: Change `5000` in `setTimeout(showPopup, 5000);` to adjust the delay.
- **Popup Message**: Edit the message inside the `<p>` tag within the popup div.

